Lesson 30: Conditional Types in TypeScript 🚀
Aaj hum seekhenge Conditional Types. Iska use karke TypeScript mein types ke basis par if-else jaisi condition laga sakte hain.
1. Conditional Type kya hota hai?
Normal JavaScript mein:
const age = 20;

if (age >= 18) {
  console.log("Adult");
} else {
  console.log("Minor");
}


TypeScript mein conditional type types ko check karta hai, runtime values ko nahi.
Iska syntax hai:
type Result = Condition extends OtherType
  ? TrueType
  : FalseType;


Yaad rakho:
- extends → check karta hai ki type doosre type ko satisfy karta hai ya nahi.
- ? → condition true hone par kaunsa type milega.
- : → condition false hone par kaunsa type milega.
2. Simple example
type Check<T> = T extends string ? "Yes" : "No";

type A = Check<string>;
type B = Check<number>;


Result:
type A = "Yes";
type B = "No";


Kyun?
- string extends string → true, isliye "Yes".
- number extends string → false, isliye "No".
3. Real-world example
Maan lo API ko ID number ya string mein mil sakti hai. Hum type ke according result decide karna chahte hain.
type ApiResult<T> =
  T extends number ? { id: T } : { value: T };

type NumberResult = ApiResult<number>;
type StringResult = ApiResult<string>;


Result:
type NumberResult = { id: number };
type StringResult = { value: string };


Yaani input type ke according output type change ho gaya.
4. Union types ke saath conditional types
type IsString<T> = T extends string ? true : false;

type Result = IsString<string | number>;


Result hoga:
type Result = true | false;


Kyun? Jab conditional type mein T ek naked type parameter hota hai, tab union ke har member par condition alag-alag apply hoti hai:
- string → true
- number → false
Is behavior ko distributive conditional types kehte hain.
5. infer ka introduction
infer conditional types ke andar kisi type ka part infer karne ke kaam aata hai.
Example: Promise ke andar ka result type nikalna.
type GetPromiseValue<T> =
  T extends Promise<infer U> ? U : T;

type A = GetPromiseValue<Promise<string>>;
type B = GetPromiseValue<number>;


Result:
type A = string;
type B = number;


infer U Promise ke andar ka type nikalta hai. TypeScript mein built-in Awaited<T> bhi Promise ke resolved type ko obtain karne ke liye use kiya ja sakta hai.
